# LocalAI for STT (Whisper) and TTS (Piper), with the LOCALAI shim. Free, local; the first start
# downloads the models.
# Engine: docker compose -f tests/ha_e2e/live/docker-compose.engines.yml --profile localai up -d --wait localai
#   then docker compose -f tests/ha_e2e/live/docker-compose.engines.yml --profile localai run --rm --no-deps init-localai,
#   which installs the backends and models below, and exits once LocalAI lists them,
#   then docker compose -f tests/ha_e2e/live/docker-compose.engines.yml --profile localai restart localai,
#   and up -d --wait localai again, for LocalAI to load the voices' configs (see init-localai in that file).
#   The Piper voices go by their gallery config names, which carry the backend; LocalAI does not list the .onnx
#   files those configs point at. --no-deps leaves LocalAI as it is, on the CPU or the GPU. The backends init-localai
#   installs are built for the image it ran against: after moving LocalAI between the CPU and GPU images, remove the
#   ha_live_engines_localai-backends volume and run init-localai again.
# Known: the device conversation and LLM-style reply cases pass. Satellites at once can fail on whisper-base
# mishearing ("whole window" for "hall window"), and long replies at once on LocalAI cutting concurrent speech
# responses short of their Content-Length. Both are LocalAI's, so one failing run on main settles a doubt.
# Serves: STT over HTTP, not streamed; TTS over HTTP, sentence by sentence.
# Backend: LOCALAI for both.
STT_OPENAI_URL=http://localai:8080/v1
STT_MODELS=whisper-base
STT_STREAMING_MODELS=
STT_REALTIME_MODELS=
STT_BACKEND=LOCALAI
TTS_OPENAI_URL=http://localai:8080/v1
TTS_MODELS=voice-en-us-amy-low voice-en-us-ryan-medium
TTS_STREAMING_MODELS=voice-en-us-amy-low voice-en-us-ryan-medium
TTS_REALTIME_MODELS=
TTS_BACKEND=LOCALAI
TTS_VOICES=
